  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...An upper ridge centered over the Southeast CONUS\nand sfc high pressure ridging in from the north will keep dry\nconditions across ENC through today and most of Friday. Gradually\nwarming and slowly increasing dewpoints today as weak synoptic\nflow allows for late day seabreeze/onshore flow to develop. One\nmore night in the 60s for tonight before TD's surge more on\nFriday as high pressure weakens and slides further offshore \nallowing low level flow to veer to sswrly ahead of an \napproaching cold front. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A cold front is progged to move in late Friday\nand Friday night. Sfc convergence and lowering heights aloft as\nshortwave energy rides over the upper ridge along with \nincreasing moisture will allow for a better chance of showers \nand perhaps a few storms acrs nrn half of the FA, with best \nchances N of Hwy 264 Friday afternoon into evening. Front slowly\nsags into srn portions of ENC Sat, with best chances for \nshowers and iso thunderstorms for srn areas on Sat. Fcst a bit \nmore muddled beyond Sat, though pops remain in the 30-50% range \nas above climo PW's will be in place along with wavy frontal \nboundary residing acrs the sern CONUS. Temps rise to above climo\nonce again Fri into early next week.",
